+/**
+ * Reverts the *top-level, real* `monorepoRoot/node_modules/yoga-layout`
+ * copy back to its pristine, shipped shape. Call this once after the
+ * esbuild bundling pass that consumes the patched files has finished
+ * (success or failure) -- see `unpatchYogaRoot`'s doc comment above for
+ * why leaving that copy patched breaks the *next* `next build`.
+ *
+ * Deliberately does **not** touch the output-tree copies under
+ * `outputDir` (the traced/`server-functions/default` roots): those are
+ * regenerated fresh by `next build`'s own file-tracing step on every
+ * `build:cf` invocation and are already baked into the esbuild bundle
+ * by the time this runs, so there is nothing to protect by reverting
+ * them too.
